    {
      "id": "69f47290-8383-5fd0-b471-02bf25d89c55",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -80,
        -620
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 640,
        "height": 620,
        "content": "## Post-visit Google review request with opt-out\n\nAsk happy clients for a review a few hours after their visit. Each client is asked once, and unsubscribes are respected.\n\n### How it works\n1. Every hour, the workflow reads the `Visits` tab of your Google Sheet.\n2. It picks rows with status `completed` whose visit ended at least `delay_hours` ago and no more than `max_age_days` ago. It skips rows already asked, rows with an invalid email, clients who opted out, and anyone already picked in the same run.\n3. No emails go out during quiet hours (in your timezone).\n4. It emails your review link and an unsubscribe link, then writes `review_requested_at` back to the row. A failed send is not marked, so it retries next hour.\n5. The unsubscribe link sets `opt_out` to TRUE on every row for that email and shows a confirmation page.\n\n### Setup\n1. Create a sheet with a `Visits` tab and the columns `visit_id, client_name, email, visit_end, timezone, status, review_requested_at, opt_out`. Format `visit_end` as plain text `yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm`.\n2. Connect Google Sheets and SMTP credentials on the red nodes.\n3. In **Config**, set the sheet URL, timezone, business name, sender email and review link. Put the same sheet URL in **Config (opt-out)**.\n4. Activate, then paste the Production URL of **Unsubscribe link** into `optout_url` in Config.\n\n### Customization\nChange the email wording in **Select visits to ask**, or change the schedule on **Every hour**."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
